.TH APKG 1 "2026-10-15" "apkg 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
apkg \- local APK installation backend
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B apkg
[global-options] command [arguments]
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B install FILE.apk ...
Install local APK, APKM, APKS or XAPK files. Calls adb install -r or Android host
pm install -r -S with APK bytes streamed through standard input.
.TP
.B list
List applications on the selected Android device.
.TP
.B info PACKAGE-ID
Show the installed versionCode.
.TP
.B remove PACKAGE-ID ...
Uninstall after confirmation; application data may be removed by Android.
.TP
.B doctor
Check backend selection and target Android SDK/ABI.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
--mode auto|adb|root, --serial SERIAL, --json, --no-progress, --yes,
--version and --help. Options precede the command.
.SH PERMISSIONS
ADB requires device authorization, not Android root.
Root mode requires Android host su and package-manager access; a Linux uid of
zero is insufficient. No backend bypasses Android signature checks.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Supports one-base split archives and universal bundletool APKS. Multi-variant
toc.pb sets require prior bundletool extraction. Unknown configuration targeting
is rejected. OBB is skipped with an explicit warning; app resources may be incomplete.
Local validation checks ZIP format and AndroidManifest.xml presence; Android
performs the installation and signature checks.
.SH EXIT STATUS
See apkm(1). A successful installation requires Android to report Success.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apkm (1),
.BR adb (1)

.SH UNINSTALL
Use Android package IDs, even when the repository uses a different application name.
No repository index or network access is required. APKM delegates removal to APKG.
All IDs are validated before confirmation or device access.
Duplicate IDs are removed once; absent applications are skipped.
Successful removal requires Android Success and a subsequent absence check.
Removal normally deletes application data. Noninteractive and JSON use require --yes.
Stop on the first failure; applications already removed remain removed.
.SH LANGUAGE
This manual is in English. Help uses Chinese for zh locales and English otherwise.
Use LANG=C apkm --help or LANG=C apkg --help to request English help.

.SH ARCHIVES
For one-base archives, select compatible ABI splits, closest known density splits,
and all language splits. Check package IDs, versions and split dependencies.
ADB uses install-multiple. Root uses install-create/write/commit and attempts
install-abandon on failure. Android validates signatures at commit.
Temporary extracted APKs are removed; original local archives are retained.
Archive installation includes an installed-version check. Limits: 2048 ZIP entries,
512 APKs, 2 GiB per entry and 8 GiB total declared uncompressed size.
